  "headline": "Indonesian Parliament Enacts Asset Seizure Law For Crime Victims",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesian Parliament Enacts Asset Seizure Law",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has passed the Asset Seizure Law, which enables the state to recover assets from various criminal activities.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The new law allows the seizure of assets derived from corruption, online gambling, and other criminal offenses to compensate victims.",
    "Legislators clarified that the statute does not include provisions for illicit enrichment regarding unexplained wealth.",
    "Parliamentary leaders have called for the establishment of two specialized bodies to support the enforcement of the new legislation."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives (DPR) has formally enacted the Asset Seizure Law, a legislative measure designed to address assets linked to corruption and other criminal acts, including online gambling, fraud, and terrorism. Officials, including House leaders Sufmi Dasco Ahmad and Habiburokhman, stated that the law aims to provide restitution to victims and act as a deterrent for perpetrators. While the legislation has received support from various groups, it has also faced scrutiny from organizations like Indonesian Corruption Watch (ICW), which criticized the exclusion of provisions regarding illicit enrichment—or unexplained wealth—among officials. To facilitate the implementation of the law, lawmakers have emphasized the necessity of creating two specialized government bodies tasked with the management and seizure of assets. The law is intended to function as a mechanism for both criminal and non-criminal asset recovery in Indonesia.",
